story_text:
# 🚦 The Fork in the Road

Code executes line by line... until it hits an **if statement**.

```cpp
if (score > 100) {
  win();
} else {
  retry();
}
```

Remember: `==` compares, `=` assigns.

buggy_code:
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    int hp = 0;
    // BUG: Assignment (=) instead of comparison (==)
    if (hp = 0) {
        std::cout << "Game Over";
    } else {
        std::cout << "Alive";
    }
    return 0;
}

solution_code:
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    int hp = 0;
    if (hp == 0) {
        std::cout << "Game Over";
    } else {
        std::cout << "Alive";
    }
    return 0;
}

