story_text:
# ⏳ Waiting Game

Use `while` when you don't know how many times to loop.

```cpp
while (energy > 0) {
    run();
}
```

buggy_code:
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    int count = 0;
    // BUG: Missing update logic, infinite loop if not fixed (or won't print expected)
    // Actually, logic: print 0 to 4
    while (count < 5) {
        std::cout << count << " ";
        // Missing increment!
    }
    return 0;
}

solution_code:
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    int count = 0;
    while (count < 5) {
        std::cout << count << " ";
        count++;
    }
    return 0;
}

